# ============================================================
# Whitelist-style .gitignore -- STRICT mode (2026-10-04).
# Default: EVERY root-level entry is ignored. Only what is
# un-ignored below is tracked; a new root-level path must be
# added here on purpose. There is no blanket directory-descent
# rule: nothing descends into the tree unless its top-level
# entry is named.
#
# Verifiable: hooks/pre-push replays FACTS.json's
# `tracked_top_levels` (and `einfacht_tracked_files`) on every
# push -- the tracked set is pinned as a value, so a stray
# `git add -f` or a re-whitelisted path turns the gate red.
# ============================================================
/*

# --- the whitelist: tracked top-level entries ---
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.toml
!/CONTEXT.md
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/config.example.toml
!/deploy/
!/docs/
!/front/
!/hooks/
!/skills/
!/src/
!/tests/

# --- explicitly untracked: the Einfacht deployment ---
# Gates, ledgers and the env carrier live local-only by decision
# (owner, 2026-10-04): a verifiable tracking whitelist is the security
# line, and Einfacht's own artifacts are not part of the published repo.
# Naming them keeps `git status` clean and the intent reviewable; the
# invariants gate forbids ever whitelisting them.
einfacht/
FACTS.json
invariants.json
Einfacht.env
STATE.md
instruments.json
doctor.json
retractions.json
questions/

# --- never tracked, even under a whitelisted directory ---
# Python bytecode: deploy/oracle/presign.py is run in place, and a stray
# __pycache__ would otherwise ride in on the deploy/** whitelist.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
